From a5bd0995ac9d21dbc47a08ec432b2601322397d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:41:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: tiled concat-transpose for the delta-net conv state

The delta-net conv-state path does ggml_transpose() straight into a dim-0
ggml_concat(), so the generic concat walks src1 with a column-major access
pattern: every consecutive invocation reads 40960 B apart (conv_channels * 4),
which is one cache line per element and one memory channel per row. This routes
that shape - and only that shape - to a 32x32 tiled kernel with a [32][33]
padded LDS tile, so the strided read is coalesced on the way in and the write
stays linear. GGML_VK_CONCAT_TRANSPOSE=0 opts out at runtime; the predicate
falls back to the generic concat when the tiled grid would exceed
maxComputeWorkGroupCount.

MEASURED EFFECT (Radeon 780M / gfx1103, Vulkan, Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated
UD-Q4_K_XL, one binary with the arms env-gated, 4 interleaved launches, 32 graph
blocks):

  CONCAT per dispatch  2550.2 us -> 2224.1 us   = -12.79%
  CONCAT per ub512 graph  122.41 ms -> 106.76 ms = -15.66 ms
  arms do not overlap: min(OFF) 2510.5 us > max(ON) 2325.7 us

The op-level win is real and unambiguous. The WHOLE-MODEL effect on this box is
not, and this commit does not claim one. CONCAT is 1.42% of the prefill graph
here (each perf block's own Total time is 8.33-9.38 s), so the end-to-end
ceiling is +0.18% - far below what a serve A/B on this hardware can resolve
(paired CI95 halfwidths +-6.7% / +-5.9% / +-31.2% on the three shapes measured).
The serve A/B accordingly read TIED on pp512@ub512, pp2048@ub512 and
pp2048@ub2048 across two counterbalanced takes, which is the arithmetically
predicted outcome and not a refutation. The upstream author's +3.3% was measured
on gfx1151, where the delta-net share of prefill is larger; that number is
neither reproduced nor contradicted here.

QUALITY / NON-DEGRADATION PROOF (this is a precondition of the merge, not a
formality):

  - reachability, on the SEAT SERVER line (-b 1024 -ub 512 -c 8192 -ctk/-ctv
    q8_0 --jinja), from an instrumented build: CONCAT_TRANSPOSE FIRED x4 with
    the gate on, 0 with the gate off. The path really is entered, and the
    opt-out really does suppress it.
  - generated text byte-identical with the gate ON vs OFF, 3/3 prompts, temp 0,
    top_k 1, presence_penalty 0 - measured with one server per arm on distinct
    ports, each proven to be a descendant of that arm's own launcher.
  - F-141 content gate GREEN 0/8 on every slot (drafted and plain).
  - test-backend-ops -o CONCAT 195/195, 0 FAIL, both arms. Noted honestly: that
    suite carries no transposed-src1 case and therefore does not exercise this
    kernel; the three checks above are what cover it.

An earlier byte-equality result for this change was withdrawn: it compared a
gate-ON server against a second gate-ON server and proved nothing. The numbers
and the proof above are the re-derived ones.

Retained under the President's win-preservation mandate of 2026-09-04
(registers/2026-09-04-local-inference-win-preservation-mandate.md): a measured,
quality-safe gain is kept and integrated even when it is statistically zero on
our own seat, and it must not be silently overwritten by a later upstream or
fork ingest without a recorded comparison and an explicit keep/replace verdict.

